Moving up to a less dangerous level is much more safe than
waiting idle on the level where you sustained the damage.
Always keep a beeline to the upstairs and bolt for it at the
first sign of danger until you have cleared and explored a level.
Once cleared the monster population is determined by
random creation and that's slow enough to be less dangerous.

Either way you do it it's a bad idea to stay in one place and
wait for a randomly generated mean monster to get to melee
range before it interupts your rest by taking the first swing.
You always want to be in a situation where you get to throw
daggers or other remote combat as a fast or mean monster
moves towards you.



